1
00:00:05,687 --> 00:00:08,657
This... is the ocean?

2
00:00:10,987 --> 00:00:15,097
Sinbad, I was actually frightened.

3
00:00:16,097 --> 00:00:19,297
What if the realities
of the outside world...

4
00:00:20,337 --> 00:00:23,337
disappointed me? What would I do?

5
00:00:24,337 --> 00:00:27,037
But that's all gone now.

6
00:00:27,937 --> 00:00:31,007
I want to know more about the world!

7
00:00:32,107 --> 00:00:34,377
So, where are we heading to next?

8
00:00:35,077 --> 00:00:36,787
Yeah, about that...

9
00:00:37,047 --> 00:00:39,687
We're heading to another small country,
like Sasan.

10
00:00:40,787 --> 00:00:44,657
We were finally approved to enter
the most secluded of the secluded regions.

11
00:00:45,787 --> 00:00:49,027
Ruled by a noble war princess,
it's a matrilineal nation.

12
00:00:50,097 --> 00:00:52,697
A municipality of the sky,
the Artemyra Kingdom.

13
00:02:26,157 --> 00:02:28,057
The Artemyra Kingdom is located

14
00:02:29,127 --> 00:02:31,127
in the southeast region of the continent.

15
00:02:31,197 --> 00:02:35,097
It is a prominent small country,
comparable to the Sasan Kingdom.

16
00:02:36,837 --> 00:02:38,367
Excluding the Dark Continent,

17
00:02:38,437 --> 00:02:41,377
their territory includes
the world's largest valley.

18
00:02:42,207 --> 00:02:45,447
Everything was obscured
and isolated from the outside world.

19
00:02:47,217 --> 00:02:48,817
Why?

20
00:02:54,987 --> 00:02:56,387
Unreal.

21
00:02:57,357 --> 00:03:00,357
Its vast terrain rejects and discourages

22
00:03:00,427 --> 00:03:02,427
any outside visitors.

23
00:03:08,067 --> 00:03:10,067
Shall we start preparing for landing?

24
00:03:10,137 --> 00:03:11,907
It's huge!

25
00:03:12,107 --> 00:03:14,007
Check out that plant!

26
00:03:14,937 --> 00:03:17,177
But it's so humid.

27
00:03:23,947 --> 00:03:24,947
A bird?

28
00:03:25,317 --> 00:03:26,587
Looks like a bird.

29
00:03:27,387 --> 00:03:29,287
But that bird's a little...

30
00:03:42,467 --> 00:03:43,337
It's gigantic.

31
00:03:45,107 --> 00:03:46,307
People?

32
00:03:53,917 --> 00:03:55,117
Impressive size.

33
00:03:55,577 --> 00:03:57,887
It's even wider than this ship.

34
00:03:58,217 --> 00:04:00,017
Look! It's coming back.

35
00:04:03,527 --> 00:04:07,057
Travelers from the outside world?
That's unusual.

36
00:04:07,357 --> 00:04:08,627
Hey there!

37
00:04:09,097 --> 00:04:11,067
What beautiful women...

38
00:04:11,297 --> 00:04:15,167
Guys! If you successfully land
in Artemyra,

39
00:04:15,237 --> 00:04:17,567
I'll show you a good time!

40
00:04:17,637 --> 00:04:18,537
What?!

41
00:04:19,037 --> 00:04:21,307
We'll see how you fare.

42
00:04:21,877 --> 00:04:25,477
Last time, the men couldn't handle
the all-nighter,

43
00:04:25,547 --> 00:04:27,577
trembling like little fawns.

44
00:04:28,317 --> 00:04:32,287
That's all men are good for
so they might as well work hard at it.

45
00:04:33,087 --> 00:04:37,127
So prove us wrong, will you? Good luck!

46
00:04:37,627 --> 00:04:39,287
Yeah, all right.

47
00:04:40,357 --> 00:04:44,567
I'll be looking forward to tonight, then.

48
00:04:47,167 --> 00:04:50,267
Idiot! I wasn't being serious.

49
00:04:54,477 --> 00:04:58,077
Now I'm a lot more excited
to get to Artemyra.

50
00:04:58,147 --> 00:05:00,377
Sinbad, I have a lot more respect for you!

51
00:05:00,447 --> 00:05:02,117
I'll be your follower forever!

52
00:05:02,177 --> 00:05:04,287
Take it easy, Ja'far.

53
00:05:06,087 --> 00:05:09,517
What was that about? He really bugs me.

54
00:05:09,587 --> 00:05:11,657
I thought he was handsome.

55
00:05:12,057 --> 00:05:14,627
Men are all talk anyway!

56
00:05:15,627 --> 00:05:17,667
Let's see if they can make it

57
00:05:17,927 --> 00:05:20,337
through this valley and get to Artemyra.

58
00:05:24,707 --> 00:05:26,937
We gotta pass through this valley today!

59
00:05:27,007 --> 00:05:29,377
Let us discover the Eden of Enchantment!

60
00:05:29,437 --> 00:05:31,407
Yeah! I'm right behind you!

61
00:05:32,707 --> 00:05:35,177
I wouldn't use up all my energy now.

62
00:05:35,247 --> 00:05:36,577
They're full of spirit.

63
00:05:36,647 --> 00:05:39,147
Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

64
00:05:48,557 --> 00:05:51,127
Why is this happening?!

65
00:05:51,667 --> 00:05:54,467
It's this way! Let's go!

66
00:05:55,137 --> 00:05:58,267
Curse you,
mountain man and ex-assassin!

67
00:05:58,607 --> 00:06:01,307
I can't do this anymore!
It's hot and I'm exhausted!

68
00:06:01,377 --> 00:06:03,077
I refuse to go any farther!

69
00:06:03,137 --> 00:06:05,407
Ja'far, let's take a break here!

70
00:06:05,477 --> 00:06:08,477
What?! Weren't we going
to pass through the valley today?

71
00:06:09,017 --> 00:06:10,987
Oh, how I envy the young...

72
00:06:11,047 --> 00:06:12,587
You're young, too!

73
00:06:14,057 --> 00:06:18,057
Carry me on your back, Hinahoho!
You can carry one or two of me.

74
00:06:20,057 --> 00:06:23,057
Heat... Humidity... Pain...

75
00:06:24,197 --> 00:06:27,697
But I'll endure it...
for my wife and son.

76
00:06:28,297 --> 00:06:30,637
Get it together, let's go!

77
00:06:35,707 --> 00:06:39,277
I'll guide you, so be mindful
of your surroundings and follow me.

78
00:06:39,677 --> 00:06:42,247
Got it, but are you sure?

79
00:06:42,317 --> 00:06:45,647
It's hot and I'm spent...

80
00:06:47,057 --> 00:06:48,287
If he keeps that up...

81
00:06:48,557 --> 00:06:52,157
Don't worry. He's the kind of man
who can do anything.

82
00:06:52,527 --> 00:06:54,357
That's why we cannot spoil him.

83
00:06:55,397 --> 00:06:57,727
Ja'far, you must trust him quite a bit.

84
00:06:57,797 --> 00:06:59,327
You never doubt him.

85
00:07:00,737 --> 00:07:03,037
It's not even about that.

86
00:07:03,667 --> 00:07:07,107
I've seen a lot as his vassal...

87
00:07:11,377 --> 00:07:13,677
I just thought of something brilliant.

88
00:07:17,047 --> 00:07:19,417
I can fly using my Djinn Equip!

89
00:07:20,557 --> 00:07:22,687
Like the ladies
who were flying on that bird!

90
00:07:23,527 --> 00:07:26,587
So, catch you later, fellas!

91
00:07:30,567 --> 00:07:33,397
What was that for, Ja'far?!

92
00:07:33,637 --> 00:07:37,167
Please understand,
we're in Artemyra territory,

93
00:07:37,607 --> 00:07:41,377
where nobody knows
about Djinn Equips or Metal Vessels.

94
00:07:42,407 --> 00:07:46,507
Flying around like that would cause them
to be unnecessarily wary of us.

95
00:07:46,707 --> 00:07:49,147
We'll lose everything!

96
00:07:49,477 --> 00:07:52,117
You're not the only one who's exhausted!

97
00:07:52,187 --> 00:07:54,817
This heat irritates me, too!

98
00:07:58,357 --> 00:08:00,157
Ja'far! That string's too tight!

99
00:08:00,227 --> 00:08:01,427
I'm choking...

100
00:08:02,157 --> 00:08:03,597
Bararaq Sei!

101
00:08:30,157 --> 00:08:33,527
-I'm done.
-Me too. I give up.

102
00:08:33,727 --> 00:08:35,297
Let's take a quick break.

103
00:08:46,337 --> 00:08:47,407
That's...

104
00:08:51,607 --> 00:08:53,277
Artemyra!

105
00:08:58,487 --> 00:09:00,657
The people of this town

106
00:09:00,717 --> 00:09:04,257
live in the tunnels dug into the cliffs.

107
00:09:04,327 --> 00:09:05,227
Yeah.

108
00:09:10,767 --> 00:09:11,927
I see.

109
00:09:12,897 --> 00:09:16,537
They use birds as their main mode
of transportation.

110
00:09:30,887 --> 00:09:32,617
Such a young child...

111
00:09:33,717 --> 00:09:36,927
We face so many unknowns
at our actual destination.

112
00:09:37,187 --> 00:09:39,787
But keep in mind
that we're not here as tourists.

113
00:09:40,397 --> 00:09:41,757
We've exchanged many letters

114
00:09:41,827 --> 00:09:44,797
to be approved for an audience
with the queen.

115
00:09:44,867 --> 00:09:48,367
I would suggest going
to the royal palace now, but...

116
00:09:50,707 --> 00:09:52,207
We stink!

117
00:09:54,607 --> 00:09:57,947
What? An inn? We don't have those here.

118
00:09:58,507 --> 00:10:01,217
We never have any visitors here.

119
00:10:01,417 --> 00:10:03,617
-Oh, no...
-But, guys,

120
00:10:05,217 --> 00:10:06,987
your stench is unbearable!

121
00:10:07,257 --> 00:10:08,717
And that's why I despise men!

122
00:10:09,287 --> 00:10:12,757
Well, is there anywhere we can bathe?

123
00:10:13,387 --> 00:10:16,497
You can perform an ablution
in the river at the bottom of the valley

124
00:10:16,557 --> 00:10:18,667
or go to the red-light district.

125
00:10:19,727 --> 00:10:20,737
Red-light district...

126
00:10:21,767 --> 00:10:25,407
I guess we have to go with the ablution.

127
00:10:25,467 --> 00:10:28,937
Ja'far, don't you think
it would be extremely rude of us

128
00:10:29,007 --> 00:10:33,477
to appear unwashed
in front of the queen?

129
00:10:34,377 --> 00:10:35,477
So...

130
00:10:35,717 --> 00:10:38,417
-let's go to the red-light district!
-Rejected!

131
00:10:38,487 --> 00:10:42,387
Ja'far! So you're saying
it's okay to stink like this?!

132
00:10:42,687 --> 00:10:45,557
We just arrived!
If you cause any trouble with a lady now,

133
00:10:45,627 --> 00:10:47,327
imagine the consequences!

134
00:10:47,557 --> 00:10:49,997
Hinahoho, the red-light district is

135
00:10:50,267 --> 00:10:52,597
a paradise where you're surrounded
by women, right?

136
00:10:52,797 --> 00:10:54,037
I read about it before!

137
00:10:54,437 --> 00:10:56,667
What in the world were you reading?

138
00:10:58,437 --> 00:11:03,277
In any case, do you see all the women
working with such high spirits?

139
00:11:04,647 --> 00:11:05,907
It seems like a good country.

140
00:11:06,377 --> 00:11:09,517
Yes, we hope to establish
a cooperative alliance with them.

141
00:11:09,577 --> 00:11:10,487
Yeah.

142
00:11:13,987 --> 00:11:16,457
We'll settle for the ablution for now.

143
00:11:16,517 --> 00:11:18,787
Yes! Let's get it out of the way.

144
00:11:21,327 --> 00:11:22,527
Excuse me.

145
00:11:22,897 --> 00:11:25,467
Oh, my, forgive me.

146
00:11:28,697 --> 00:11:31,037
What a big lady...

147
00:11:35,977 --> 00:11:38,477
You've come a long way.

148
00:11:39,077 --> 00:11:41,877
Her Excellency is waiting.
This way, please.

149
00:11:43,917 --> 00:11:45,887
Her Excellency is not in her best mood.

150
00:11:46,387 --> 00:11:48,617
Please be mindful of what you say.

151
00:11:55,757 --> 00:11:58,497
Your Excellency,
we are extremely delighted

152
00:11:58,567 --> 00:12:00,537
for the honor
to have an audience with you.

153
00:12:01,437 --> 00:12:04,607
I am Sinbad,
the proprietor of Sindria Company.

154
00:12:05,467 --> 00:12:09,007
It's an international trading company
based in the Reim Empire.

155
00:12:09,807 --> 00:12:13,977
We are here in hopes to establish trade
with your country.

156
00:12:17,047 --> 00:12:20,487
Your Excellency,
do we appear inept in any way?

157
00:12:21,457 --> 00:12:23,787
If something is bothering you...

158
00:12:31,727 --> 00:12:34,597
It's been a while
since I've had male guests.

159
00:12:44,107 --> 00:12:45,977
Go ahead, entertain me.

160
00:12:47,547 --> 00:12:52,987
I am Mira Dianus Artemina,
queen of Artemyra.

161
00:12:53,787 --> 00:12:57,757
Far too many visitors have looked down
on me for being a woman.

162
00:12:58,457 --> 00:13:02,657
That's why I chastise them from the start.

163
00:13:03,897 --> 00:13:07,137
Every one of you is a man.

164
00:13:07,897 --> 00:13:09,697
In letters prior to this meeting,

165
00:13:09,767 --> 00:13:13,137
the company's advisor was
a woman named Rurumu.

166
00:13:13,807 --> 00:13:18,877
She's pregnant right now
so she had to stay behind. Today...

167
00:13:19,477 --> 00:13:21,777
Well, that's a drag. Then leave.

168
00:13:22,617 --> 00:13:24,717
I have no desire to speak to men.

169
00:13:24,787 --> 00:13:27,957
Men are only here to produce
our offspring, that's it.

170
00:13:28,617 --> 00:13:31,927
How can I speak about diplomacy
with such people?

171
00:13:31,987 --> 00:13:34,997
Please, give us a chance.

172
00:13:35,057 --> 00:13:36,927
Enough! I told you to leave.

173
00:13:38,567 --> 00:13:39,997
Please wait, Your Excellency.

174
00:13:41,197 --> 00:13:44,007
I will never betray you.

175
00:13:44,807 --> 00:13:47,507
I only intend to do our best to benefit

176
00:13:47,877 --> 00:13:50,547
this country and Your Excellency.

177
00:13:54,747 --> 00:13:56,647
Please believe me.

178
00:13:57,917 --> 00:13:58,817
Your Excellency.

179
00:14:05,187 --> 00:14:06,687
So, that's how...

180
00:14:07,557 --> 00:14:11,097
you've been seducing women
all over the world, right?

181
00:14:12,227 --> 00:14:15,567
I'm different from other men.

182
00:14:15,767 --> 00:14:17,767
You're wrong.

183
00:14:18,607 --> 00:14:24,547
You're not the only one to say
that you're different from other men.

184
00:14:24,977 --> 00:14:27,247
That's... for me to decide.

185
00:14:29,477 --> 00:14:31,687
Seduction is a man's shallow wit.

186
00:14:32,887 --> 00:14:38,487
I'll show you the terror you'll face
when you deceive women.

187
00:14:41,057 --> 00:14:43,827
You're mistaken!
We never intended to deceive you.

188
00:14:43,897 --> 00:14:45,867
-Take them away.
-Yes!

189
00:14:53,107 --> 00:14:55,977
Can this woman also be...?!

190
00:14:57,037 --> 00:15:00,647
Oh, so you're also a King's Candidate,
master of a Djinn.

191
00:15:00,917 --> 00:15:03,117
A Metal Vessel sorcerer...

192
00:15:04,147 --> 00:15:06,987
You're not just a boor.

193
00:15:07,987 --> 00:15:11,927
But that still doesn't change the fact
that you offended me.

194
00:15:12,787 --> 00:15:15,957
Hey! We don't know
what the others are hiding!

195
00:15:16,027 --> 00:15:17,597
Strip them all!

196
00:15:19,297 --> 00:15:21,767
-What are you doing?!
-Hey, that's...!

197
00:15:21,837 --> 00:15:23,267
Take everything off! All of it!

198
00:15:28,577 --> 00:15:32,577
"Valley of the Dead,"
our country's deepest and darkest.

199
00:15:33,307 --> 00:15:36,117
No one survives this fall.

200
00:15:36,977 --> 00:15:38,817
You shall starve and crumble to dust.

201
00:15:39,247 --> 00:15:42,187
No! I don't want to die here!

202
00:15:42,257 --> 00:15:46,627
Oh, my, look how sturdy you look
without any clothes.

203
00:15:48,557 --> 00:15:52,997
If you return from the valley,
let me show you a good time.

204
00:15:54,067 --> 00:15:56,137
But I doubt you can!

205
00:15:56,597 --> 00:15:57,267
What?

206
00:15:58,007 --> 00:15:58,867
What?

207
00:16:00,137 --> 00:16:02,207
Sin! Guys!

208
00:16:04,647 --> 00:16:08,017
He's powerless,
even as a Metal Vessel sorcerer.

209
00:16:08,917 --> 00:16:11,687
You're one of the Imuchakk,
the tribe of the extreme north.

210
00:16:12,247 --> 00:16:16,987
We'll be examining
your unusual physique.

211
00:16:17,727 --> 00:16:20,027
You're not trying to dissect me, are you?!

212
00:16:20,797 --> 00:16:24,197
-What a great body.
-So burly...

213
00:16:24,267 --> 00:16:26,127
Look at those muscles!

214
00:16:28,997 --> 00:16:32,137
I'll make you experience something
even more terrifying than death.

215
00:16:46,087 --> 00:16:47,687
Hey, is everyone okay?

216
00:16:47,757 --> 00:16:50,387
Yes, seems like we survived it.

217
00:16:50,657 --> 00:16:52,957
My body hurts all over though!

218
00:16:53,227 --> 00:16:57,057
It's a miracle
that we even survived that fall.

219
00:16:57,827 --> 00:16:59,967
We gotta figure out a way back.

220
00:17:00,937 --> 00:17:03,167
That's right! We gotta go back alive!

221
00:17:03,667 --> 00:17:05,867
-Hey, Mystras.
-Yes?

222
00:17:06,307 --> 00:17:10,207
That lady said something before she
pushed you over the cliff, didn't she?

223
00:17:10,277 --> 00:17:11,907
What did she tell you?

224
00:17:11,977 --> 00:17:14,177
What? It was nothing.

225
00:17:14,247 --> 00:17:17,277
No, you're hiding something! I know it!

226
00:17:17,847 --> 00:17:19,717
I'm not hiding anything!

227
00:17:19,787 --> 00:17:21,987
-You are!
-No, I'm not!

228
00:17:22,057 --> 00:17:25,157
-You are! You are!
-No, I'm not! No, I'm not!

229
00:17:25,227 --> 00:17:26,087
Shut it!

230
00:17:26,727 --> 00:17:31,027
Why don't you hide those instead?

231
00:17:31,827 --> 00:17:32,697
Hide what?

232
00:17:32,867 --> 00:17:35,697
Those things that
can't be seen on-screen!

233
00:17:35,767 --> 00:17:36,797
Screen?

234
00:17:39,937 --> 00:17:43,177
The leaves aren't settling in place.

235
00:17:43,237 --> 00:17:46,207
You gotta use a vine to keep it in place.

236
00:17:47,307 --> 00:17:49,217
All right! That's perfect.

237
00:17:51,187 --> 00:17:53,217
Is this acceptable, Ja'far?

238
00:17:54,787 --> 00:17:57,057
I guess so...

239
00:17:57,457 --> 00:18:00,827
All right!
Let's get to searching the area!

240
00:18:01,097 --> 00:18:02,197
Yeah!

241
00:18:06,067 --> 00:18:07,837
It sure is the Valley of the Dead.

242
00:18:08,297 --> 00:18:11,137
This is going to be a struggle to capture.

243
00:18:11,807 --> 00:18:15,907
The surface of the walls are covered
with moss. It's impossible to climb.

244
00:18:16,377 --> 00:18:18,977
There's no sign of animals either.

245
00:18:19,707 --> 00:18:22,377
There's absolutely no way out.

246
00:18:25,487 --> 00:18:30,087
That's right, we haven't eaten anything
since we got to this country.

247
00:18:31,457 --> 00:18:35,327
Actually... I have some emergency food.

248
00:18:36,427 --> 00:18:39,127
Knights of Sasan keep emergency food

249
00:18:39,197 --> 00:18:42,097
in their turbans for times of crisis.

250
00:18:42,997 --> 00:18:47,337
It's a custom to prepare for
the eventuality of being held captive.

251
00:18:47,907 --> 00:18:49,777
Please split it between yourselves.

252
00:18:50,237 --> 00:18:52,907
No, this is yours, Mystras.

253
00:18:53,177 --> 00:18:54,777
You should eat one.

254
00:18:55,247 --> 00:18:58,487
-What? But...
-It's okay.

255
00:19:02,017 --> 00:19:05,087
I was actually starving to death myself.

256
00:19:05,827 --> 00:19:07,057
Thank you.

257
00:19:09,297 --> 00:19:10,527
Delicious!

258
00:19:12,127 --> 00:19:13,397
Ja'far.

259
00:19:15,767 --> 00:19:17,367
This one's yours.

260
00:19:18,337 --> 00:19:21,507
I can't take any food from you...

261
00:19:22,207 --> 00:19:23,477
the youngest one here.

262
00:19:24,307 --> 00:19:25,177
Sin...

263
00:19:27,177 --> 00:19:30,317
Thank you very much, but I'm okay.

264
00:19:31,017 --> 00:19:35,317
During my years as an assassin,
I often went days without food.

265
00:19:35,857 --> 00:19:37,257
Sin, you should eat that jer--

266
00:19:37,317 --> 00:19:40,257
Oh, really? Then I'll eat it!

267
00:19:41,327 --> 00:19:43,497
Hey! What do you think you're doing?!

268
00:19:43,557 --> 00:19:45,227
He said it was mine.

269
00:19:46,497 --> 00:19:49,037
Can't you follow Ja'far's example?!

270
00:19:49,097 --> 00:19:51,107
Aren't you embarrassed as our leader?!

271
00:20:05,947 --> 00:20:07,217
What's that sound?

272
00:20:14,127 --> 00:20:16,827
Wake up, both of you!
Snakes everywhere!

273
00:20:19,867 --> 00:20:23,197
I see various kinds,
large, small and poisonous.

274
00:20:23,267 --> 00:20:25,167
This is like a swamp of snakes!

275
00:20:25,437 --> 00:20:26,967
What should we do?

276
00:20:27,167 --> 00:20:30,277
Ja'far, Mystras! Live on for me!

277
00:20:31,577 --> 00:20:34,347
I wish I could've chosen
my own place of death.

278
00:20:35,377 --> 00:20:37,217
Surrounded by beautiful women,

279
00:20:37,277 --> 00:20:41,017
delicious food, delicious wine,
and other delicious things...

280
00:20:41,087 --> 00:20:42,917
What are you saying?

281
00:20:42,987 --> 00:20:45,487
-What?
-Good grief.

282
00:20:46,027 --> 00:20:49,057
It's unlike you to spill your guts.

283
00:21:06,377 --> 00:21:08,447
You're only acting weak

284
00:21:08,517 --> 00:21:10,117
because you're hungry.

285
00:21:10,617 --> 00:21:13,287
But that's an easy fix!

286
00:21:18,427 --> 00:21:21,897
Let's restore our energy by eating this!

287
00:21:22,127 --> 00:21:23,227
Ja'far...

288
00:21:23,427 --> 00:21:25,167
You're... going to eat that?

289
00:21:25,997 --> 00:21:29,437
I've strangled and eaten many of these
during my assassin years.

290
00:21:29,497 --> 00:21:31,107
It's packed with nutrients,

291
00:21:31,167 --> 00:21:34,277
and as long as we cut the neck,
you can eat the poisonous ones, too.

292
00:21:36,207 --> 00:21:38,047
Let's eat!

293
00:21:38,107 --> 00:21:39,007
Yes!

294
00:21:39,077 --> 00:21:42,547
Take your time, there's plenty of them!

295
00:21:50,517 --> 00:21:53,387
Sinbad and his crew worked
in earnest to survive.

296
00:21:54,527 --> 00:21:57,227
They ate snakes, built fires,

297
00:21:57,297 --> 00:22:01,397
gathered vegetation to construct
a house that kept the rain and wind out.

298
00:22:02,337 --> 00:22:04,137
They worked as the sun rose

299
00:22:04,607 --> 00:22:06,637
and slept when the sun set.

300
00:22:08,207 --> 00:22:11,307
While living a life revolved
around the sun,

301
00:22:11,377 --> 00:22:15,047
their instincts as animals
were coming back.

302
00:22:16,447 --> 00:22:17,477
They then...

303
00:22:19,687 --> 00:22:21,487
successfully adapted...

304
00:22:23,457 --> 00:22:25,087
to this extreme situation.

